<wpml-config>

	<!--
		WPML configuration for MBN Theme.

		WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
		Every mbn-theme block is a dynamic, self-closing block: all of its copy lives
		in JSON attributes inside the block comment, not in inner HTML. WPML cannot
		guess which attributes are text, so without this file it registers no
		translatable strings for these blocks at all - the WPML Translation Editor
		shows an empty job and Spanish pages render the English attribute values.

		AFTER EDITING THIS FILE
		WPML caches theme config. Re-read it via
		WPML > Support > Troubleshooting > "Reset and load the configuration files",
		then re-save (or re-queue) any page whose blocks changed.

		CONVENTIONS USED BELOW
		  translated : visible copy, alt text, and navigational link targets
		               (so Spanish CTAs can point at /es/ pages)
		  omitted    : attachment IDs, media URLs (use WPML Media Translation),
		               colors, alignment, class names, layout flags, anchors
	-->

